WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.370
How is it we should
measure information

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.800
in a way that applies
to any communication

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.550
system you can think of?

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.806
Human, animal, or alien?

00:00:12.806 --> 00:00:17.840
[CHIRPING]

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.150
Well, let's return to the late
19th century, where at the time

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.324
we were focused, as we
are today, on speed.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:26.710
[PIANO MUSIC]

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.275
And one goal to
improve speed was

00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:32.580
to design a machine which
allowed the operators to input

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.320
letters, which we can think
of as primary symbols,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.530
and have the machine automate
the lower level signaling

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.326
events, such as
pulses of electricity,

00:00:42.326 --> 00:00:45.390
what we can call
secondary symbols.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.460
And machines can be driven
by some clock source,

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.670
allowing it to generate
a precise and rapid pulse

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.850
stream, which
presumably would run

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.430
much faster than any human hand.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.570
And one great example of
this was the Baudot Multiplex

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.520
System.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.459
And the design was put
into service in 1874.

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:06.880
And it built off the
same conceptual ideas

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.520
we've seen in the
shutter telegraph.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.870
It consisted of five
keys, which could

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.112
be played in any combination.

00:01:13.112 --> 00:01:14.070
Think of it as a chord.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.960
Each combination would
represent a unique message.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.960
With five notes, each
either on or off,

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:29.070
you can play 2 the power of
5, or 32 different chords.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.030
The code assigned the
32 different chords

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.980
to each letter of the
alphabet, with the leftover

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:39.080
used for carriage returns,
new line, and spaces.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.390
So the operator would
literally play letters,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.300
and their machine
would automatically

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:49.720
output a pulse stream
representing the letters.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:59.360
ANNOUNCER: Like this for letter
T. Or like this for letter R.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:05.830
Or like this for letter B.
So we have an output signal

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:10.740
containing various combinations
of DC impulses, a signal that

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.940
accurately represents
the message

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.235
type from a teletypewriter.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.360
NARRATOR: Behind the counter,
the mechanical nerves

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.340
of the system change
words to holes on tape,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.420
and the holes on tape to
electrical impulses speeding

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.050
over the wires.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:28.180
SPEAKER 1: Notice at the
lowest level, this system

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.150
is exchanging either
the presence or absence

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:36.040
of electrical current in a
sequence divided using a clock.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.250
So, how fast can our
internal clocks run?

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.520
Well, the limiting
speed was not the clock.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.040
Then and today, the
speed of transmission

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.070
was physically limited
by the minimum spaces

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:52.790
between these impulses,
or the pulse rate.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.050
And this problem
plagued engineers

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.590
who were testing
underground submarine cables

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.060
using the existing
Morse code system.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.500
And it's similar to an
echo, or a sustained note.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.620
If one sends dots too fast
over a long undersea circuit,

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.580
they will run together
at the receiving end.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.240
Because the symbol we
received at the far end

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.860
of the circuit will
be a slightly longer,

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:24.020
smoothed out rise and
fall, not an exact replica.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.960
And sending pulses
too fast results

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.830
in inter-symbol interference.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:33.560
This occurs, for example, when
the longer flow of a current

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.630
bleeds into the
next time division,

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:39.000
and perhaps reverses a 0 to a 1.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.170
So even if we're
automating the detection

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:44.800
of these current levels,
there is a fundamental limit

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.190
to how far we can squeeze
two pulses together.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:51.380
And this is the same
problem Alice and Bob ran

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:58.400
into with their string
communication system, which

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.030
we called the
maximum pluck speed.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.280
If they plucked any faster
than two plucks per second,

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.420
they noticed they started
to bleed together,

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.740
and they got confused.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:13.630
So this is called
the symbol rate.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.500
Remember, a symbol
can be broadly defined

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.440
as the current state of
some observable signal which

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.580
persists for a fixed
period of time.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:29.060
Whether you are using fire,
sound, electrical current,

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.660
anything, a signaling event
is simply a change from one

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.160
state to another.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.950
So the symbol rate is the
number of signaling events which

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.460
can be squeezed
together in one second.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.025
[BEEPING]

